 ### Fixed
 
+- **Call hierarchy follows trait constructors.** Constructor calls point to the composed trait implementation, including inherited constructors and named aliases, and incoming calls retain those construction sites. Ambiguous trait aliases do not invent a target. Contributed by @thinkycz.
+
 - **Private member identity.** References and rename distinguish a parent's private declaration from a child's independent namesake while retaining legal lexical access and public override families. Nested trait conflict selection preserves the selected implementation. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
 
 - **Rename refuses occupied names.** Member and class renames preserve distinct declarations, PHP case rules and private inheritance boundaries. Case-only changes and unrelated owners remain available. Parent trait members also follow their effective visibility and class declaration precedence, while inaccessible accesses still report their owning class. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
